Great answer to Trump, but hard to cram more into her head in terms of
quotes to memorize tonight. Still we should come back to it.

On Sunday, January 17, 2016, <podesta.mary@gmail.com> wrote:

> Wow.  The full passage is even more powerful and apt than I thought.
>
> On Jan 17, 2016, at 11:26 AM, John Podesta <john.podesta@gmail.com
> <javascript:_e(%7B%7D,'cvml','john.podesta@gmail.com');>> wrote:
>
> Here's the quote
>
> ---------- Forwarded message ----------
> From: *Kristina Costa* <kcosta@hillaryclinton.com
> <javascript:_e(%7B%7D,'cvml','kcosta@hillaryclinton.com');>>
> Date: Sunday, January 17, 2016
> Subject: Read this message to the end
> To: John Podesta <john.podesta@gmail.com
> <javascript:_e(%7B%7D,'cvml','john.podesta@gmail.com');>>
>
>
> It is from a commencement address he gave at Oberlin in 1965.
> http://www.oberlin.edu/external/EOG/BlackHistoryMonth/MLK/CommAddress.html
>
>
>
> Now it is true that the geographic togetherness of our world has been
> brought into being, to a large extent, through modern man's scientific
> ingenuity. Modern man, through his scientific genius, has been able to
> dwarf distance and place time in chains. Yes, we've been able to carve
> highways through the stratosphere, and our jet planes have compressed into
> minutes distances that once took weeks and months. And so this is a small
> world from a geographical point of view. What we are facing today is the
> fact that through our scientific and technological genius we've made of
> this world a neighborhood. And now through our moral and ethical commitment
> we must make of it a brotherhood. *We must all learn to live together as
> brothers - or we will all perish together as fools. This is the great issue
> facing us today. No individual can live alone; no nation can live alone. We
> are tied together.*
>
>
>
> *From:* John Podesta [mailto:john.podesta@gmail.com]
> *Sent:* Sunday, January 17, 2016 10:58 AM
> *To:* Kristina Costa <kcosta@hillaryclinton.com>
> *Subject:* Fwd: Read this message to the end
>
>
>
> Want to ck this quote out?
>
> ---------- Forwarded message ----------
> From: <podesta.mary@gmail.com>
> Date: Sunday, January 17, 2016
> Subject: Read this message to the end
> To: John Podesta <john.podesta@gmail.com>
>
>
> Jim Greenfield ended an amazing homily just now with a quote from Martin
> Luther King Jr saying in more or less these exact words
>
> Unless we all find a way to live together, we will all die together as
> fools.
>
>  Useful in the campaign and today's debate? Definitely timely.  Might want
> to check it out.
>
> Hope all is well.
>
> Love
> Mary
>
>

